      "narrative": "The question lands. Mara Venn's cup stops halfway to her lips. She holds it there, frozen, and you catch the flicker of something behind her eyes \u2014 surprise, quickly masked, then calculation.\n\nShe sets the cup down. Slowly.\n\n\"The lock,\" she repeats. Her voice is careful now, stripped of the casual dismissal from a moment ago. Her sharp eyes study you with renewed interest.\n\nShe nods once, a small admission. \"Toran Vex.\" She gestures with her chin toward the ink-stained clerk still dabbing at his papers. \"He's the lockwright who kept the Ash Gate's mechanism working for years. Before it was sealed. Before the key vanished.\"\n\nToran's head snaps up at the sound of his name. His face pales beneath the ink smudges. \"I\u2014 I was just the maintenance man. I didn't *design* it, I just\u2014\" He stops, swallows. His cuffs are ringed with black stains, his fingers nervously twisting a rag.\n\nMara watches him, then turns back to you. \"If anyone knows the gate's bones, it's him. But he's not the talking type.\" Her tone carries a warning \u2014 not for you, but for *him*. A reminder.\n\nToran looks down at his ruined papers, saying nothing more.\n\nThe rain continues its drumming against the shutters."
    },
