      "narrative": "The name leaves your mouth and hangs in the damp air, swallowed by the vast grey silence of the field.\n\n*\"Old Bram.\"*\n\nNo echo. The gate's black stone drinks the sound. The grass whispers against itself. Somewhere behind you, in the village, a dog barks once and falls quiet.\n\nYou wait. The drizzle beads on your shoulders, on your lashes. The wind shifts, carrying the faint smell of wet earth and cold stone. The cavity in the gate \u2014 that empty, fist-sized recess \u2014 stares back at you like a dead eye.\n\nNothing moves. Nothing answers.\n\nThe cloak at your feet lies still in the grass. A crumpled shape, travel-worn, dark with moisture. Whoever left it here did so recently \u2014 the fabric hasn't begun to rot, hasn't been claimed by the mud. It simply lies there, discarded, as if its owner shrugged it off and walked away.\n\nThe gate offers no secrets to a shouted name. Whatever Old Bram knew, he took with him into the ground."
    },
